  "independent_review": {
    "sha256": "7e2a33b5a01c979e4d579cecc2b635e4ad60df04d8e7b3205e675449bce9c7ce",
    "text": "# Independent sandbox launcher V2 delta review\n\nPatch SHA-256 `59df6bbc8c8803489701a3f3481861a3b7d977946b1e8489fbe5d587b0563922` differs from V1 only by rejecting the `NetworkServiceSandbox` disable-feature spelling and adding its negative control. All 17 before/after source identities match the respective canonical and isolated files; static syntax checks and strict apply check pass. Independently invoked the helper with that exact feature switch and observed rejection before its callback.\n\nThe retained V2 ARM helper run reports namespace and seccomp-BPF sandboxing enabled, and the V2 lifecycle log reports all 18 controls passed with zero exit. Those are bounded local observations; the browser and full lifecycle suite were not independently rerun here. The custom-argument policy remains a finite denylist, not a general guarantee against all security-affecting flags. The direct dump-dom timeout, untested Karma/CI/x64 behavior, and fixed overlay/table/Karma source-proof successor requirements described in review-v1 remain unchanged. No canonical files were changed.\n"
  },
